    "facts": "The appellant got married with the son of de-facto complainant-respondent no.2 on 05.07.2014.\nThe appellant was issued with a passport during her stay at her matrimonial home on 21.08.2014.\nAn application was filed, jointly with her husband, by the appellant on 17.03.2020 seeking issuance Poonam Bhupatbhai Odedra vs State Of Gujarat on 15 September, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/61417792/\n1 of residency permit of the United Kingdom.\nA case was registered on 25.08.2020 in F.I.R.\nNo.11218001200011 for the offences punishable under Section(s) 498A, 323, 406, 420, 506(2),\n120B, 109, 494 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 and Section(s) 3 and 5 of the Dowry Prohibition Act,\n1961.\nBoth the appellant and her husband initiated divorce proceedings against each other which are stated to be pending in the United Kingdom.\n",
    "ANALYSIS": "The registration of the FIR, at the instance of respondent no.2, is certainly an abuse of the process of law, warranting interference by invoking Section 482 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973.\nIt is to be noticed that the complaint was given by respondent no.2 as a counter blast to the case registered against his son.\nThe application was made by the appellant after her marriage seeking a passport during her stay at the matrimonial home.\nThe alleged occurrence was in the year 2014 whereas the complaint was given in the year 2021.\n",
